r of the Maratha kingdom."},{"iast":"sambhājī","name":"Sambhaji","devanagari":"संभाजी","dictionary_gloss":"Named after Shambhu (Shiva); the second Maratha ruler."},{"iast":"pṛthvīrāja","name":"Prithviraj","devanagari":"पृथ्वीराज","dictionary_gloss":"King of the earth."},{"iast":"tilaka","name":"Tilak","devanagari":"तिलक","dictionary_gloss":"Sacred mark on the forehead; ornament, the best of its kind."},{"iast":"mohanadāsa","name":"Mohandas","devanagari":"मोहनदास","dictionary_gloss":"Servant of Mohan (Krishna)."},{"iast":"vivekānanda","name":"Vivekananda","devanagari":"विवेकानन्द","dictionary_gloss":"Bliss of discernment; the monk Swami Vivekananda."},{"iast":"baṅkima","name":"Bankim","devanagari":"बंकिम","dictionary_gloss":"Gracefully curved, bent; an epithet of Krishna (as in Bankim Bihari)."},{"iast":"sukhadeva","name":"Sukhdev","devanagari":"सुखदेव","dictionary_gloss":"God of happiness; giver of joy."},{"iast":"madanamohana","name":"Madanmohan","devanagari":"मदनमोहन","dictionary_gloss":"One who enchants even Kamadeva; a name of Krishna."},{"iast":"rāmaprasāda","name":"Ramprasad","devanagari":"रामप्रसाद","dictionary_gloss":"Grace (blessing) of Rama."},{"iast":"kālidāsa","name":"Kalidas","devanagari":"कालिदास","dictionary_gloss":"Servant of Goddess Kali; name of the great Sanskrit poet."},{"iast":"cāṇakya","name":"Chanakya","devanagari":"चाणक्य","dictionary_gloss":"Descendant of Chanaka; name of the strategist-minister of Chandragupta Maurya."},{"iast":"suśrut","name":"Sushrut","devanagari":"सुश्रुत","dictionary_gloss":"Well heard, renowned."},{"iast":"tyāgarāja","name":"Tyagaraja","devanagari":"त्यागराज","dictionary_gloss":"King of renunciation; the great Carnatic composer, named after Shiva of Tiruvarur."},{"iast":"nāmadeva","name":"Namdev","devanagari":"नामदेव","dictionary_gloss":"God of the divine name; also the Marathi saint-poet."},{"iast":"samīra","name":"Samir","devanagari":"समीर","dictionary_gloss":"Breeze, gentle wind."},{"iast":"jalada","name":"Jalad","d